# Authentication

Purpose:
  Authentication

Skill: Authentication

ID:
  SKILL-CROSS-SECURITY-AUTH

Domain:
  cross-cutting/security

Use:
  implementing authentication systems

Apply:
  intermediate
  senior
  security
  access-control

Requires:
  security-fundamentals
  jwt-or-oauth

Avoid:
  plaintext-passwords
  weak-tokens
  session-fixation
  password-in-url

Level:
  L2

Status:
  STABLE

Maturity:
  MATURE

Risk:
  HIGH

Review:
  2026-08

Version:
  1.0

EvidenceLevel:
  HIGH

SearchKeys:
  authentication
  auth
  jwt
  oauth
  oidc
  password
  login

TechnologyLifecycle:
  Current: MATURE

HumanDoc:
  docs/skills/cross-cutting/security/authentication.md

Evidence:
  - OWASP Authentication Guide
  - JWT RFC 7519
  - Production experience

Rules:
  [A1] Use bcrypt or Argon2 for password hashing.
  [A2] Use HTTPS for all authentication endpoints.
  [A3] Use JWT with short expiry and refresh tokens.
  [A4] Implement rate limiting on login endpoints.
  [A5] Use multi-factor authentication (MFA).
  [A6] Store tokens in HttpOnly cookies for web apps.
  [A7] Implement account lockout after failed attempts.
  [A8] Use OAuth 2.0 / OIDC for third-party auth.

Pros:
  - Secure access
  - User trust
  - Compliance

Cons:
  - Complexity
  - User friction
  - Token management

Alternatives:
  - Session-based auth
  - Magic links
  - Passkeys

State: +

